      "writtenOn": "2024-03-11T13:59:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What if these two conditions change in the next boot of the same VM? (ex: perhaps due to host being compromised)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 145,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 146,
        "endChar": 80
      },
      "revId": "e7bd85d00674fce13f41472b15a9d4ad2e016889",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c7399c55_bd78e878",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/main.rs",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 146,
      "author": {
        "id": 1897307
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-11T15:20:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The only possibility of these changing on the next boot is if host is compromised or an update from Sk not supported to Sk supported OS happen.\n\nDowngrading from Secretkeeper to Non secretkeeper case will lead to secret mechanism changing from V2 -\u003e V1 (ie Sealing CDIs will be used to derive secrets \u0026 instance.img will be required). We differentiate the sealing secrets of V2 \u0026 V1 to avoid possibility of this leading to leaking secrets.\n\n\nUpgrading from Secretkeeper to Non secretkeeper case would  let the boot succeed but the final secrets would be a mix of Sealing CDIs and randomly generate secrets (that are stored in Sk). This will essentially be equivalent to get_new_secrets.",
      "parentUuid": "d173a156_615615ba",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 145,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 146,
        "endChar": 80
      },
      "revId": "e7bd85d00674fce13f41472b15a9d4ad2e016889",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
