      "side": 1,
      "message": "So what\u0027s the policy for flipping that build flag?\n\nAFAICT, given that\n```\nSealing_CDI \u003d KDF(H(Auth + Mode + Hidden))\n```\nthen, the host would now be (indirectly) in control of the CDI of non-`SecretkeeperProtection`-capable guests, right?\n\nWe previously mandated that the instance.img was encrypted (by pvmfw), to guarantee the confidentiality and integrity of the salt (`Hidden`); I don\u0027t get how `llpvm_changes` changes this requirement for those \"legacy\" use-cases?",
      "range": {
