      "writtenOn": "2024-03-11T15:20:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e what\u0027s the policy for flipping that build flag\n\nThe llpvm_changes is tied to Android 24Q3 release\n\n\n\u003e the host would now be (indirectly) in control of the CDI of non-SecretkeeperProtection-capable guests, right?\n\nAs we discussed, we need to mix the `defer_rbp` into hidden inputs, that is a blocker ofcourse. I\u0027ll add a TODO.\n\n\n\u003e We previously mandated that the instance.img was encrypted (by pvmfw), to guarantee the confidentiality and integrity of the salt (Hidden)\n\n\nThe encryption of salt added nothing to the security, the malicious host can use the target VM\u0027s encrypted salt. It was really the combination of authenticated encryption of the code hashes \u0026 /chosen/avf,new-instance that prevented leaking the security.",
      "parentUuid": "1660cc8d_8a6914c5",
      "range": {
