      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e [1] seems to ensure that /avf/untrusted exists when llpvm_changes is on.\n\nThanks for the pointer.\n\nAFAICT, this CL would break the basic `crosvm run --protected`, right? IMO, we shouldn\u0027t assume that pVMs are only spawned through `virtmgr`, unless absolutely necessary (not the case here).\n\n\u003e Pierre-Clement, when do you think SK can be off while llpvm_changes is on?\n\nMy point was that pvmfw shouldn\u0027t abort the boot if `/avf/untrusted` is missing, unless it needs it. And it doesn\u0027t need it if the guest doesn\u0027t have `Capability::SecretkeeperProtection`.",
      "parentUuid": "f57f0353_f3fe7797",
