      "writtenOn": "2024-03-11T15:20:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Won\u0027t this make pvmfw panic for non-Sk use-cases \u0026 And it doesn\u0027t need it if the guest doesn\u0027t have Capability::SecretkeeperProtection\n\n\nThe untrusted node is mandatory to start any pVM. It has the `instance_id` which is mandatory for all OSes (including rialto) \u0026 replaces the salt in instance.img. This is irrespective of `Capability::SecretkeeperProtection`. \n\nThere is nothing pvmfw can do in absence of id other than aborting the boot (The behaviour should be similar to TRNG failures).\n\nTo clarify potential confusion here:\n1) Secretkeeper is optional (devices may/maynot ship it)\n2) Instance-id change is mandatory with 24Q3, so llpvm_changes \u003d\u003e /untrusted node will be present. This replaces our dependency on salt in instance.img\n3) If Secretkeeper is not supported in 24Q3 releases, instance.img will be needed for code hashes \u0026 all, but the salt field will be obsolete.\n\n\n\u003e AFAICT, this CL would break the basic crosvm run --protected, right\n\nThe additional `--device-tree-overlay` will be needed to make it work. What was the lagacy crosvm behavior if an virtio-blk device with Instance.img MAGIC_HEADER was not provided?\n\n\nI dont think there is a better solution to removing the apparent fragility between virtmg/pvmfw/Microdroid MM. This project touches multiple components \u0026 this is expected. (combined with trust released \u0026 build time flagging, which is considerably dropped code readability).\n\n\nIf you\u0027re concern is bummbling appropriate errors, I can change instance_id() to return `FdtError::NotFound` but the caller will endup mapping it to a reboot reason \u0026 I think `InvalidFdt` is the most appropriate one, so I dont see the immediate benefit.",
